{"success": true, "message": "Test details sent successfully", "data": {"test": {"_id": "69de4b8aa20fc16230f14b57", "analysisVideoCdn": "yt", "exam": ["605dfcb2f226ac25a8bd5fef"], "ctype": null, "position": 0, "order": 12, "enableCalculator": false, "isContinuousQuestion": false, "reattemptAvailable": false, "singleSectionMultipleSubjects": false, "timeRestricted": false, "title": "Capacitance - Test 4", "description": "Previous Year Questions as Chapter Test", "syllabus": "This test contains questions from all topics of this chapter included in the JEE Main syllabus. It includes a mix of questions from PYQs of JEE Main 2019 - 2025.", "totalTime": 40, "totalQuestions": 20, "totalMarks": 80, "bonusQuestions": null, "bonusMarks": null, "startDate": "2026-04-15T03:30:00.000Z", "endDate": "2027-04-30T00:00:00.000Z", "type": "free", "class": "605df635a37b7025c438d685", "instruction": "608289ffb160b022e9442c83", "subjects": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "totalMarks": 80, "bonusMarks": 0, "totalQuestions": 20, "bonusQuestions": 0, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a420"}], "sections": [{"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a41d", "title": "Physics Numerical", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d90", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3a4", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae3"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b475a"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4efa"], "question": {"text": "<p>The charge accumulated on the capacitor connected in the following circuit is ______<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"></mo><mi>μC</mi></math>.</p><p>(Given <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>150</mn><mo> </mo><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fc8eb7317-479a-4c7c-be6a-eb879e2cee31.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 153px;\"/>"}, "options": [{"id": "9b1177", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3a5"}, {"id": "b48977", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3a6"}, {"id": "b5d55f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3a7"}, {"id": "789b68", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3a8"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3a9", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae3"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f42"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f11"], "question": {"text": "In the given circuit.<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>=</mo></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></math>. The charge stored on capacitor <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp; ______&nbsp; &nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>.<br /><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fcae6bf64-5e50-47a4-a6f7-fc4670e21f19.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 347px; height: 241px;\" />"}, "options": [{"id": "a896f3", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3aa"}, {"id": "8cfadf", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3ab"}, {"id": "33fc5a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3ac"}, {"id": "2ee6ad", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3ad"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3ae", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae3"], "topics": ["60e5678e499d1e49588f927b"], "concepts": ["6117b5e3478ae845c43c5e02"], "question": {"text": "A parallel plate capacitor with width <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>, length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>&nbsp;and separation between the plates of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math> is connected to a battery of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>. A dielectric slab of dielectric constant <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math> having length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>, width <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> and thickness <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi></math> is inserted between the plates of parallel plate capacitor. The electrostatic energy of this system will be _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#1013;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>. (Where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#1013;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is the permittivity of free space)"}, "options": [{"id": "6966c1", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3af"}, {"id": "ce52fd", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3b0"}, {"id": "8b40a3", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3b1"}, {"id": "a98ad8", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3b2"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3b3", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae3"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b77"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b40"], "question": {"text": "A parallel plate capacitor of capacitance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>200</mn><mi>&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></math> is connected to a battery of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>200</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;A dielectric slab of dielectric constant <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> is now inserted into the space between plates of capacitor while the battery remain connected. The change in the electrostatic energy in the capacitor will be __________&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>.</mo></math>"}, "options": [{"id": "bfbdb5", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3b4"}, {"id": "524149", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3b5"}, {"id": "7a0f3a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3b6"}, {"id": "e2afc7", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3b7"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3b8", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae3"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b77"], "concepts": ["617aa9d0ef3fe65ad8e82070"], "question": {"text": "A time varying potential difference is applied between the plates of a parallel plate capacitor of capacitance $2.5 \\mu \\mathrm{~F}$. The dielectric constant of the medium between the capacitor plates is 1 . It produces an instantaneous displacement current of 0.25 mA in the intervening space between the capacitor plates, the magnitude of the rate of change of the potential difference will be _____ $\\mathrm{Vs}^{-1}$."}, "options": [{"id": "815c48", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3b9"}, {"id": "a54582", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3ba"}, {"id": "f141ff", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3bb"}, {"id": "97509c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3bc"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3bd", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae3"], "topics": ["60e5678e499d1e49588f927b"], "concepts": ["617aa9d0ef3fe65ad8e82072"], "question": {"text": "<p>A parallel plate capacitor with plate area&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;and plate separation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi></math>&nbsp;is filled with a dielectric material of dielectric constant&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo></math> The thickness of the dielectric material is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo></math> where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F78c088e9-5c75-4687-a8b4-43e2a32c0d2d-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 128px;\" /></p><p>Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;be the capacitance of the system for&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mi>d</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>d</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;respectively. If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;F</mi></math>,&nbsp;the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#956;F</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "66b684", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3be"}, {"id": "f6fca0", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3bf"}, {"id": "171bc2", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3c0"}, {"id": "ed9582", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3c1"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3c2", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae3"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b475a"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b470e"], "question": {"text": "The electric field between the two parallel plates of a capacitor of $1.5 \\mu \\mathrm{F}$ capacitance drops to one third of its initial value in $6.6 \\mu \\mathrm{s}$ when the plates are connected by a thin wire.\nThe resistance of this wire is _____$\\Omega$. (Given, $\\log 3=1.1$ )"}, "options": [{"id": "350ce8", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3c3"}, {"id": "b1bd48", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3c4"}, {"id": "aa7ca5", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3c5"}, {"id": "95ed94", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3c6"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3c7", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae3"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f42"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f11"], "question": {"text": "<p>Four identical rectangular plates with length, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> and breadth, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> are arranged as shown in figure. The equivalent capacitance between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is _______.</p><p>(Round off to the Nearest Integer)</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F65bd1939-6cea-4e12-9039-d7aa9a1b497d-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 214px; height: 215px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "a35de4", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3c8"}, {"id": "581d9c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3c9"}, {"id": "b9ed11", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3ca"}, {"id": "6d78c8", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3cb"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3cc", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae3"], "topics": ["60e5678e499d1e49588f927b"], "concepts": ["60e5678c499d1e49588f9254"], "question": {"text": "<p>A composite parallel plate capacitor is made up of two different dielectric materials with different thickness (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>) as shown in figure. The two different dielectric material are separated by a conducting foil <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi></math>. The voltage of the conducting foil is _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>.</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fa6e4366c-5f4d-4015-b004-498db9e6a610-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 120px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "741e24", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3cd"}, {"id": "8758fc", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3ce"}, {"id": "20efdc", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3cf"}, {"id": "d27c44", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3d0"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3d1", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae3"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b77"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b40"], "question": {"text": "A parallel plate capacitor consisting of two circular plates of radius 10 cm is being charged by a constant current of 0.15 A . If the rate of change of potential difference between the plates is $7 \\times 10^8 \\mathrm{~V} / \\mathrm{s}$ then the integer value of the distance between the parallel plates is $\\left(\\right.$ Take, $\\left.\\epsilon_0=9 \\times 10^{-12} \\frac{\\mathrm{~F}}{\\mathrm{~m}}, \\pi=\\frac{22}{7}\\right)$ ________ $\\mu \\mathrm{m}$."}, "options": [{"id": "cda4ae", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3d2"}, {"id": "761762", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3d3"}, {"id": "518612", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3d4"}, {"id": "1e6ab0", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3d5"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3d6", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae3"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b475a"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4efa"], "question": {"text": "<p>In an electrical circuit drawn below the amount of charge stored in the capacitor is _______ <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>μC</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F21628cfd-ecfc-4400-a6da-2fbfbae6132e.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 200px; height: 165px;\"/>"}, "options": [{"id": "ed52fd", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3d7"}, {"id": "ad1d60", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3d8"}, {"id": "96d64b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3d9"}, {"id": "687ffc", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3da"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3db", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae3"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f42"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f11"], "question": {"text": "<p>The equivalent capacitance between points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> in below shown figure will be _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></math>.</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F7cae1e0d-e073-4508-a214-5075d14a2097-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 79px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "e8e9ae", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3dc"}, {"id": "dc18aa", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3dd"}, {"id": "07b09e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3de"}, {"id": "035cf3", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3df"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3e0", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae3"], "topics": ["60e5678e499d1e49588f927b"], "concepts": ["6117b5e3478ae845c43c5e02"], "question": {"text": "A parallel plate capacitor has plate area <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></math> and plate separation of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;The space between the plates is filled up to a thickness <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> with a material of dielectric constant of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo></math> The resultant capacitance of the system is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>pF</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>85</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>.&nbsp;The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> to the nearest integer is ______."}, "options": [{"id": "1a6e97", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3e1"}, {"id": "b80afc", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3e2"}, {"id": "ef309e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3e3"}, {"id": "eafa01", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3e4"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3e5", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae3"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b475a"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b470e"], "question": {"text": "<p>Two parallel plate capacitors <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> each having capacitance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;F</mi></math> are individually charged by a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> D.C. source. Capacitor <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> is kept connected to the source and a dielectric slab is inserted between it plates. Capacitor <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> is disconnected from the source and then a dielectric slab is inserted in it. Afterwards the capacitor <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> is also disconnected from the source and the two capacitors are finally connected in parallel combination. The common potential of the combination will be _____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>.</p><p>(Assuming Dielectric constant <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></math>)</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "447567", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3e6"}, {"id": "a43622", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3e7"}, {"id": "1bbc7d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3e8"}, {"id": "28f414", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3e9"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3ea", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae3"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b77"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b40"], "question": {"text": "A capacitor of capacitance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math> and potential <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi></math> has energy <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi><mo>.</mo></math> It is connected to another capacitor of capacitance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>C</mi></math> and potential <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>V</mi></math>. Then the loss of energy is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mi>E</mi></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math> is _______."}, "options": [{"id": "2bf578", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3eb"}, {"id": "cf5d20", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3ec"}, {"id": "45d2c3", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3ed"}, {"id": "1c4638", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3ee"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3ef", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae3"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f42"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f11"], "question": {"text": "<img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2FJMyY2RBIuUPkY4Mfe2TaxhQgG4KzANtwG3mfjDCutGg.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"/><br/>Space between the plates of a parallel plate capacitor of plate area $4 \\mathrm{~cm}^2$ and separation of (d) 1.77 mm, is filled with uniform dielectric materials with dielectric constants (3 and 5) as shown in figure. Another capacitor of capacitance 7.5 pF is connected in parallel with it. The effective capacitance of this combination is ________ pF. $\\left(\\right.$ Given $\\left.\\varepsilon_0=8.85 \\times 10^{-12} \\mathrm{~F} / \\mathrm{m}\\right)$"}, "options": [{"id": "3ddc67", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3f0"}, {"id": "7ed5c4", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3f1"}, {"id": "2c8504", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3f2"}, {"id": "422855", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3f3"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3f4", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae3"], "topics": ["60e5678e499d1e49588f927b"], "concepts": ["617aa9d0ef3fe65ad8e82072"], "question": {"text": "A parallel plate capacitor with air between the plate has a capacitance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>pF</mi></math>. The separation between the plate becomes twice and the space between them is filled with a medium of dielectric constant <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></math>. Then the capacitance becomes <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>pF</mi></math>. The value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;is____."}, "options": [{"id": "1e39db", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3f5"}, {"id": "f73a6f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3f6"}, {"id": "67aeb9", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3f7"}, {"id": "24aa29", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3f8"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3f9", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae3"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b475a"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4efa"], "question": {"text": "<p>As show in the figure, in steady state, the charge stored in the capacitor is _____<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&times;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>.</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2Fa43429db-419e-4530-9592-f099bb90dccb-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 185px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "a27cab", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3fa"}, {"id": "2626be", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3fb"}, {"id": "7ff88e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3fc"}, {"id": "f690de", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3fd"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3fe", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae3"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b77"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b40"], "question": {"text": "<p>A parallel plate capacitor whose capacitance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>14</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>pF</mi></math> is charged by a battery to a potential difference <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> between its plates. The charging battery is now disconnected and a porcelain plate with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn></math>&nbsp;is inserted between the plates, then the plate would oscillate back and forth between the plates with a constant mechanical energy of _______&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>pJ</mi><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>(Assume no friction)</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "240851", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a3ff"}, {"id": "da2d26", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a400"}, {"id": "b1b094", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a401"}, {"id": "b02bfc", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a402"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a403", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60ced3330e34b73944ddfae3"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f42"], "concepts": ["60e2fb5666f9ce3f243b4f11"], "question": {"text": "<p>A parallel plate capacitor is made up of stair like structure with a plate area A of each stair and that is connected with a wire of length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi></math>, as shown in the figure. The capacitance of the arrangement is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>15</mn></mfrac><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>, The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is _____ .</p><p><img src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Fjee_main%2F33650a16-f05e-4fce-8841-32e58b694a58-image.png?alt=media\" style=\"width: 160px; height: 208px;\" /></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "a2f282", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a404"}, {"id": "c3ff23", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a405"}, {"id": "7b0062", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a406"}, {"id": "2fb4ce", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f522ee0e063d926a407"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283c623cf4b3ad8f125e5", "title": "JEE Numerical", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45:27.79